1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:03,937
Southern California needs more affordable homes,

2
00:00:03,787 --> 00:00:06,841
and every one of them starts with a piece of land.

3
00:00:07,441 --> 00:00:11,988
In just four Orange County cities, the state's housing goals call for

4
00:00:11,838 --> 00:00:14,473
more than 13,000 very-low-income homes.

5
00:00:15,073 --> 00:00:19,296
But the facts that decide whether a site can work are scattered across

6
00:00:19,146 --> 00:00:22,788
parcel maps, zoning layers, hazard zones and permit records.

7
00:00:23,288 --> 00:00:26,820
Meet CivicAcre: affordable housing site intelligence.

8
00:00:27,820 --> 00:00:31,213
It brings 22 public data sources together on one map,

9
00:00:31,063 --> 00:00:34,333
so teams can see which sites deserve a closer look.

10
00:00:34,933 --> 00:00:39,930
Start with an interactive map of 470 housing-element sites across

11
00:00:39,780 --> 00:00:43,063
Irvine, Santa Ana, Costa Mesa and Anaheim.

12
00:00:43,863 --> 00:00:47,932
Choose the cities you care about, search by address or parcel number,

13
00:00:47,782 --> 00:00:50,375
and narrow the list with one-click filters.

14
00:00:51,775 --> 00:00:55,591
Every site is rated for open land, housing capacity,

15
00:00:55,441 --> 00:00:59,399
size, transit and opportunity, and screened for flood,

16
00:00:59,249 --> 00:01:02,149
fire, landslide and contamination risk.

17
00:01:02,749 --> 00:01:06,914
Open a parcel to see its facts, how its score was built,

18
00:01:06,764 --> 00:01:12,148
and a preliminary screen of state housing pathways like SB 9 and AB 2011.

19
00:01:12,848 --> 00:01:15,427
Compare promising sites side by side.

20
00:01:18,327 --> 00:01:21,268
Then save a shortlist, track your due diligence,

21
00:01:21,118 --> 00:01:23,303
and export a printable site report.

22
00:01:26,003 --> 00:01:30,814
CivicAcre connects housing, zoning, transit and environmental data in

23
00:01:30,664 --> 00:01:34,462
one place, with every source and assumption on screen.

24
00:01:35,062 --> 00:01:38,234
So nonprofit developers and city planners can decide,

25
00:01:38,084 --> 00:01:41,084
faster, which sites deserve their next phone call.

26
00:01:42,084 --> 00:01:45,996
CivicAcre. Smarter land discovery. Stronger communities.

